> I'm not perfectly sure what "single-valued
> mapping" intended but it probably should mean
> that for any given input -- which may have any
> number of components -- it yiields a unique
> output ("value").  So, the domain might be a
> set
> of ordered n-tuples, not just single items.  If
> that is what you want, a function from input to
> output, then {fancu} is probably your best
> word. 
> Or some compound of it, if there are details
> tht
> need special treatment.
